# HarnessLab Quality Gate

Before creating ANY git commit in this repository, the agent MUST run:

```bash
uv run python scripts/check_package_layout.py
uv run pytest
uv run ruff check
```

Only proceed with `git commit` if all succeed. If any fails, fix the
issue first and re-run the gate.

This is also enforced by the local pre-commit hook
(`.pre-commit-config.yaml`), but the agent should never rely on the hook
alone — running the gate explicitly produces clearer error context and
matches the workflow defined in `AGENTS.md`.

The `package-check` hook validates `[tool.hatch.build.targets.wheel]`
`packages` and `force-include` paths so deleted assets (e.g. legacy
`web/static/`) cannot drift from `pyproject.toml`. CI runs `uv build` for
the same reason on every push/PR (`/.github/workflows/ci.yml`).

## On contract changes

If a change touches any stable Port (`ModelPort`, `PolicyPort`, `ToolPort`,
`SessionStorePort`, `MemoryStorePort`, `SpanRecorderPort`, `ClockPort`,
`IdPort`), the same commit MUST also update:

- `docs/architecture/overview.md`
- `docs/architecture/data-model.md` (if data shape changed)
- `docs/architecture/tool-runtime.md` (if tool/policy behavior changed)
- Relevant contract tests under `tests/`
